<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Changzi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Changzi is a county in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanxi">Shanxi</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, now part of the city of Changzhi. In 386 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murong-yong">Murong Yong</a> made it the capital of the Western Yan, one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sixteen-kingdoms">Sixteen Kingdoms</a>. In 394 the Later Yan ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murong-chui">Murong Chui</a> besieged and took the city and executed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murong-xianbei">Murong</a> Yong, ending the Western Yan.</p></div>
